Explanation of the fix:

- We keep track of the last rendered projection in `lastProjection_`.  
- In `reset()`, which is invoked whenever the layer’s source/style is changed, we flush out the old textures.  
- In `renderFrame()`, at the very top, we detect if the projection has changed since the last frame; if so, we again flush the cache so no stale tiles are reused.
